1
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,100
Sheldon, your food is getting cold.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,330
I'll eat later.

3
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:07,350
Right now, I'm suckling at

4
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:10,140
the informative bosom of mother physics.

5
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:14,180
It's hot when Sheldon talks dirty.

6
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,870
So, I found this Web site

7
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:19,300
where you send them pictures,

8
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,370
they sculpt your head

9
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:22,250
and make an action figure out of you.

10
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,270
How awesome is that?

11
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:24,410
Oh, let me see.

12
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:25,470
Yeah, you can pick your wardrobe.

13
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,340
You can even choose your accessories.

14
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:31,950
Leonard, you can get a little asthma inhaler.

15
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:35,630
Oh, this is neat.

16
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:38,590
Think about all the action figures we've bought over the years.

17
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,160
It would be kind of cool to have ones that look like us.

18
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,650
Don't you think?

19
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,110
Yeah, if that's your idea of what's cool,

20
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,800
you should get one.

21
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,820
Yeah, so, I'm out.

22
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:53,320
What do you think, Sheldon?

23
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,490
Want an action figure that looks just like you?

24
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:57,490
Would it come with kung-fu grip?

25
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:58,540
No.

26
00:00:58,570 --> 00:00:59,860
Don't waste my time.

27
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,880
You get that these are personalize action figures.

28
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,180
Honey, if you want one, just get one.

29
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:08,910
-You're still out, right? - Yep.

30
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:38,870
A hush falls over the crowd

31
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:40,790
as Cooper studies the board.

32
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,190
He makes his move.

33
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,700
He's dividing both sides by "I."

34
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,030
He's adding back the coefficient.

35
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:49,330
He has a value for "P."

36
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:50,430
He's plugging that back in.

37
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:51,430
He takes the derivative,

38
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:52,900
and he solves the equation.

39
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:53,540
The crowd goes wild.

40
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:55,740
Nobel! Nobel!

41
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:56,770
Cooper?

42
00:01:57,870 --> 00:01:58,610
Nobel.

43
00:01:58,610 --> 00:01:59,630
Kripke.

44
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:02,900
Don't look at my board.

45
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:06,070
What's that?

46
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:08,710
That's a drawing of a really cool train.

47
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:10,550
Don't look at that, either.

48
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:11,780
What do you want?

49
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,270
I have some bad news.

50
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,130
You're working on a grant proposal for a new fusion reactor.

51
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:19,100
I'm working on a grant proposal for a new fusion reactor.

52
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:22,740
The university is only allowed to submit one proposal.

53
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:24,770
So they asked you to pack up your things and ship out.

54
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:27,230
That's hard cheese, Barry.

55
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,950
You're one of the good ones.

56
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:32,870
No, they're making us work together.

57
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:36,000
That's ridiculous.

58
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,220
I am one of the great minds of our generation.

59
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:40,290
I work on a level so rarified

60
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,930
you couldn't even imagine it.

61
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:44,340
I said stop looking at my cool train!

62
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:49,440
Kind of a strange place

63
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,450
to put a picture of you and Bernadette.

64
00:02:51,450 --> 00:02:55,760
Well, I wanted everybody to know I love my wife.

65
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:59,990
And nobody to know I forgot to turn off the laser.

66
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:04,550
They're here.

67
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:06,480
Our action figures have arrived.

68
00:03:06,490 --> 00:03:09,210
This is the best $500 I've ever spent.

69
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:11,640
$1,000 on action figures?

70
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:12,810
How can you afford that?

71
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:14,210
Easy-- his family's loaded,

72
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:16,150
and Bernadette has a great job.

73
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:19,470
My wife came with both fun bags and money bags.

74
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:24,880
Say hello to an exact scale model of me.

75
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:33,190
Oh, I'm not dark chocolate.

76
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:35,940
I'm melt-in-your-mouth caramel.

77
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:38,730
Oh, man.

78
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,030
Look at my nose.

79
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,510
Maybe it's a shipping problem.

80
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:49,740
- What? - Yeah.

81
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:51,300
Maybe Wesley Snipes and Toucan Sam

82
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,810
just got action figures that look like you guys.

83
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:57,190
This sucks.

84
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,870
I can't believe I wasted all that money.

85
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:02,070
Aw, and my girlfriend wouldn't let me get one.

86
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:04,520
Look at my face.

87
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,660
Do I look smug? I feel smug.

88
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,680
I hate it when you make me sit through all the credits.

89
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,590
Well, sometimes there's a secret ending,

90
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,210
like in The Avengers.

91
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:18,820
Yeah, but I don't think that's going to happen

92
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:21,510
in a documentary about the Holocaust.

93
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:25,850
They could show bloopers.

94
00:04:28,170 --> 00:04:29,210
Oh, no.

95
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:30,760
What is that?

96
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,470
That is Sheldon's

97
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:35,330
"I'm unhappy and about to destroy the planet" music.

98
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,870
Come on, let's just go to your place.

99
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:39,990
Well, wait, if he's unhappy, shouldn't we talk to him?

100
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:41,130
"Shouldn't we talk to him?"

101
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:43,360
Have you learned nothing in six years?

102
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:52,200
You doing okay, sweetie?

103
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:57,260
There is ominous music playing,

104
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,690
and there is an afghan over my head.

105
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:00,620
I don't know where you're from,

106
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,220
but where I'm from, that means I'm not doing okay.

107
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,550
Want me to make you some tea?

108
00:05:05,610 --> 00:05:07,940
Tea is for when I'm upset. I'm not upset.

109
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:10,740
The university's forcing me to work with Kripke.

110
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,280
I'm outraged.

111
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:14,880
So, cocoa?

112
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,480
Yes, cocoa.

113
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,630
Do you have any idea what it's like to be paired

114
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:23,000
with someone who's so incredibly annoying?

115
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,170
Oh, teacher! Me! Me!

116
00:05:28,030 --> 00:05:29,490
See, I did all this great work,

117
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,430
and now he's just going to come along and ruin it.

118
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:34,440
I am angrier than ever and filled with despair.

119
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,080
What beverage do you make for that?

120
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:39,550
Oh... no, no, no, I know this.

121
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,320
Hot apple cider with cinnamon sticks?

122
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,350
Yes, hot apple cider with cinnamon sticks!

123
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,710
What the frig, Cooper?

124
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:54,670
We were supposed to meet in my office a half an hour ago.

125
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:57,240
And yet, now you're in my office.

126
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:59,340
Point, Cooper.

127
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,760
Welcome to the Thunderdome, Kripke.

128
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:05,350
We agreed to exchange copies of our work.

129
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:06,670
Let me see yours.

130
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:09,060
Why don't you show me yours first.

131
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:12,400
You think I just fell off the turnip truck?

132
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,520
We exchange at the same time.

133
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:18,470
How do I know you're not going to take my ideas

134
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:20,050
and publish them as your own?

135
00:06:20,050 --> 00:06:21,720
How do I know you're not going to do that with mine?

136
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,720
Yeah, because I'm not interested

137
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,670
in getting published in Mad magazine.

138
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:29,440
Zingers fly fast in the Thunderdome, Barry.

139
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,710
Are we going to do this or not?

140
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:33,630
Thank you.

141
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:35,980
So, we read each other's work, meet again tomorrow?

142
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,360
Fine.

143
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,190
Nice try. This is blank paper.

144
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:45,880
And I am sure it's still more valuable

145
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:47,500
than whatever's in here.

146
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:50,050
Cough it up, Cooper.

147
00:06:50,050 --> 00:06:51,390
Very well.

148
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:59,820
If this one's blank, too, I'm going to be furious.

149
00:07:03,030 --> 00:07:04,030
Fine.

150
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:14,060
You!

151
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:16,220
Always bet on black.

152
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:20,030
Get that waste of money out of my face.

153
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:21,440
It's only a waste of money

154
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,450
if we don't play with them.

155
00:07:23,450 --> 00:07:25,140
He's right, dawg.

156
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,930
Please, I'm working.

157
00:07:28,930 --> 00:07:31,880
You know, there is a way we can get action figures

158
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,480
to look exactly like us.

159
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,140
Oh, yeah? How's that?

160
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:37,890
Two words: 3-D printer.

161
00:07:37,890 --> 00:07:39,440
Wait, maybe it's three words.

162
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:40,800
No, hang on.

163
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:44,030
Okay, one word, a letter and a number and...

164
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,600
maybe a hyphen.

165
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,740
3-D printer.

166
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:51,150
I have always wanted a 3-D printer.

167
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:52,470
Of course you have.

168
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:53,600
They're an engineer's dream.

169
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:54,740
Anything you can design,

170
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:56,910
a 3-D printer can make out of plastic.

171
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,320
Yeah, but they're so expensive.

172
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,280
Oh, come on.

173
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,380
You deserve one.

174
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:02,880
You've worked hard to find a woman

175
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,180
who makes a lot of money.

176
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:08,790
Well, the prices have been coming down.

177
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:10,020
Oh, true.

178
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:12,060
They're practically giving them away.

179
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:15,090
You know, in exchange for money.

180
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:18,760
And we can make stuff we need for work with it.

181
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,960
Prototypes of my CAD/CAM designs,

182
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,190
specialized tools...

183
00:08:22,190 --> 00:08:24,030
Not to mention Malibu Koothrappali

184
00:08:24,030 --> 00:08:25,970
and his totally bitchin' dream house.

185
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,440
We don't need Malibu Koothrappali's dream house.

186
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,680
Really, smart guy?

187
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,420
Where's he supposed to park his sweet little Corvette?

188
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:40,670
The monkey in my tobacco study has taken to smoking a pipe.

189
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,000
I'm supposed to remove his brain to examine,

190
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,270
but it's hard because now he reminds me of my uncle.

191
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,690
You've been awfully quiet tonight.

192
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,030
Is everything okay?

193
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:55,260
I'm fine.

194
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:58,000
All right, well, how was work today?

195
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,740
Did you exchange your research with Kripke?

196
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,340
Yes.

197
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:06,420
Sheldon, what's going on?

198
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:11,260
I read his research, and...

199
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,830
it's leaps and bounds ahead of mine.

200
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:18,010
Which means the mommy of the smartest physicist

201
00:09:18,010 --> 00:09:22,010
at the university is not my mommy as I had thought.

202
00:09:23,090 --> 00:09:24,780
It's his mommy.

203
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,540
Sheldon, I wish there was something I could do

204
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,380
to make you feel better.

205
00:09:31,810 --> 00:09:33,760
May I offer you a consoling hug?

206
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:36,470
What do we have to lose?

207
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:44,800
How's that?

208
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,120
I feel like I'm being strangled by a boa constrictor.

209
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,220
Why'd you stop?

210
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:02,600
Come on, Sheldon! We're going to be late!

211
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,990
I can't go in today. I'm sick.

212
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:07,600
You're not sick.

213
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:08,870
You just don't want to face Kripke.

214
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:11,200
No, look.

215
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:16,430
128.

216
00:10:18,350 --> 00:10:20,120
See?

217
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,880
What did you do, put this in your tea?

218
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,580
Oh, dear.

219
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:27,140
Now I'm not even smarter than you.

220
00:10:28,170 --> 00:10:30,450
Sheldon, Kripke's not smarter than you.

221
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:32,190
You just got stuck on a wrong path.

222
00:10:32,190 --> 00:10:33,560
Happened to Einstein.

223
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,690
He got stuck on the unified field theory for decades.

224
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:37,820
Oh, don't play the Einstein card.

225
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:40,050
His great breakthroughs happened when no one knew anything.

226
00:10:40,050 --> 00:10:42,330
So everything was a great breakthrough.

227
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,040
Sheldon Lee Cooper,

228
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,920
I do not have time for this nonsense.

229
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,780
Now, go put your clothes on, get in the car,

230
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:49,370
and lets go to work.

231
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:52,390
All right, geez.

232
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,800
What a grouch.

233
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:58,640
How did I do that?

234
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,360
I got to remember how I did that.

235
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:04,940
Do you realize, by owning a 3-D printer,

236
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:07,800
we are reclaiming the manufacturing process

237
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:12,180
and taking jobs back from sweatshops in China?

238
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,770
I think this thing was made in China.

239
00:11:16,190 --> 00:11:18,160
Eh, what can you do?

240
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:20,880
Ooh, I-I think it's done.

241
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,510
It worked!

242
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:27,050
We printed a whistle.

243
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:30,070
Amazing.

244
00:11:30,070 --> 00:11:32,040
You realize these things go for 25 cents a pop

245
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,120
at a party store.

246
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,870
And we made it in only three hours.

247
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,050
Sounds just like store-bought.

248
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:44,570
Okay, give me a superhero pose,

249
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,850
and I will scan you into the computer

250
00:11:46,850 --> 00:11:48,780
for your action figure.

251
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:51,200
Oh, I wish I was in better shape.

252
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:54,550
Stop holding your stomach in.

253
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:57,350
I'll give you a six-pack with the computer.

254
00:11:57,350 --> 00:11:59,080
Oh, okay, great.

255
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,420
Now I can look like Val Kilmer as Batman

256
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:04,060
instead of Val Kilmer as he looks today.

257
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:09,640
All right, you can suck it in a little bit.

258
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:14,300
Cooper, we have a problem.

259
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,240
Your work is really not

260
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,580
at a level I expected it to be.

261
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,020
I know.

262
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,880
Go ahead, mock me.

263
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:24,570
Just use small words so I understand.

264
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,480
Don't play dumb with me.

265
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,170
We both know what your problem is.

266
00:12:29,170 --> 00:12:31,080
We do?

267
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,620
You have a girlfriend.

268
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:33,800
So?

269
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,720
So my work would suffer, too,

270
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:38,700
if I was getting laid all the time.

271
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:44,870
Yes.

272
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:48,810
That is the reason.

273
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,580
